# DRAFT: nothing has been released yet. The version, date and DOI are filled in at release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CommonsWire, please cite it as below, and credit the newsrooms as each row asks."
type: software
title: "CommonsWire: a living, full-text corpus of openly licensed news"
abstract: >-
  CommonsWire collects the full text of news articles whose publishers allow redistribution
  (public domain and Creative Commons licenses), checks each source's rights on its own pages,
  and keeps every article's license and credit line with it. It is updated every day and adds
  validated coded variables (topic, frame, types of sources quoted, tone) for communication and
  journalism research.
authors:
  - family-names: Kraishan
    given-names: Obada
    affiliation: "College of Media and Communication, Texas Tech University"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/obadaKraishan/commonswire"
keywords:
  - news
  - corpus
  - journalism
  - communication research
  - creative commons
  - content analysis
